  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Le Festival Plage is a beach restaurant at 10 promenade de la Mer in Menton, among the private beaches lining the Garavan bay. Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur Tourisme describes a panoramic view of the Mediterranean, a clean and elegant setting, generous dishes made from fresh produce and recipes that showcase the nearby sea. You can hire a sunbed for the day or half-day.</p>
      <h2>With your dog</h2>
      <p>None of the official sources read (Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur Tourisme page, Menton Riviera & Merveilles tourist office lists) says that dogs are allowed at the tables or on the terrace of this restaurant. Other establishments along the promenade de la Mer show "Pets accepted" on their tourist office page, but not this one: the rule must therefore be asked directly before you come.</p>
      <p>The town of Menton's website also reminds visitors of the beach rule: only Hawaï beach, towards Garavan, and Casino beach are open to dogs; all others are banned to animals, even on a leash. This rule applies to the public beaches; it doesn't say what applies to the restaurants' private beach areas, which is one more reason to call.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: for a swim, I head for Hawaï beach, towards Garavan, which the town opens to dogs. For the meal, I call first.</div>
      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Promenade de la Mer, along Les Sablettes beach, is a wide pedestrian area for a walk before or after the meal, according to the tourist office. Hawaï beach and Casino beach are the two public beaches open to dogs.</p>
